## Why This Is Asked
Tests that exercise keyboard accessibility demonstrate familiarity with a11y concepts and deterministic testing approaches for beginners.

## Key Concepts
- Keyboard navigation and focus management
- ARIA roles and attributes (role=dialog, aria-label, aria-live)
- Test determinism with seeded localStorage and deterministic delays

## Code Example

```javascript
// Example test outline in Cypress
describe('Keyboard accessibility for notes', () => {
  it('navigates via Tab, opens modal, saves, edits, deletes, and persists', () => {
    // seed
    window.localStorage.setItem('notes', JSON.stringify([
      { id: 1, title: 'Note 1', body: 'Body 1' },
      { id: 2, title: 'Note 2', body: 'Body 2' }
    ]));

    cy.visit('/');

    // Tab through list and verify focus
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.focused().should('have.attr', 'role', 'listitem');

    // Open create modal with keyboard
    cy.get('[data-testid="create-button"]').focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[role="dialog"]').should('be.visible');

    // Create note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').type('New Note');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-body"]').type('New Body');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Edit existing note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus().type('{enter}');
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-title"]').clear().type('Edited Title');
    cy.get('[data-testid="save-button"]').click();

    // Delete note
    cy.get('[data-testid="note-item"]').first().focus();
    cy.get('[data-testid="delete-button"]').click();

    // Verify persistence after reload
    cy.reload();
    cy.window().then(win => {
      const notes = JSON.parse(win.localStorage.getItem('notes'));
      expect(notes).to.have.length(2);
    });
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests for offline-first flows are common in modern web apps and require practical use of network emulation, event queues, and deterministic conflict handling. This question probes hands-on ability to design reliable E2E tests that stay robust under connectivity changes.

## Key Concepts

- Offline-first UX and service workers
- Network emulation in Playwright or Cypress
- Backend API mocking and idempotent sync
- Deterministic conflict resolution policy
- Data seeding for repeatable tests

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright test skeleton
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('offline create and sync with deterministic merge', async ({ browser }) => {
  const context = await browser.newContext();
  const page = await context.newPage();
  // seed data via API (omitted for brevity)
  // go offline
  await context.setOffline(true);
  await page.goto('https://app.example');
  await page.fill('#title', 'Offline note');
  await page.fill('#body', 'content');
  await page.click('#save');
  await expect(page.locator('#status')).toHaveText('Queued');
  // go online and sync
  await context.setOffline(false);
  const resp = await page.waitForResponse('/api/notes');
  // assume server returns created note with serverId
  await expect(resp.status()).toBe(201);
  // verify note appears and is synced
  await expect(page.locator('.note-title').last()).toHaveText('Offline note');
  // optional conflict scenario in a second tab would be tested similarly
});
```

